.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ox-gate 1  "ox-gate " 
.SH NAME
ox\-gate \- Manage gates
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBox\-gate\fR [\fB\-\-approver\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIACTION\fR] [\fIGATE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage gates
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-approver\fR \fI<APPROVER>\fR
Approver identity
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Approval reason or rejection message
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR [default: Oxymakefile.toml]
Oxymakefile path
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIACTION\fR]
Subcommand: list (default), approve, reject
.TP
[\fIGATE\fR]
Gate to approve/reject: its name (the `[gate.<name>]` key) or the numeric id shown by `ox gate list`
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
    ox gate list
    ox gate approve qc_check \-\-approver alice \-\-reason "metrics look good"
    ox gate reject qc_check \-\-reason "coverage too low"
    ox gate approve 3                      # by id, when two runs wait on the same gate
